    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3489A\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Islip,\ncounty of Suffolk, to accept an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes from the East Islip Fire District\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the town of Islip, county of Suffolk, to\naccept an application for exemption from real property taxes from the\nEast Islip Fire District.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Islip to accept an application for\nexemption from real property taxes with respect to a portion of the\n2021-2022 assessment roll and with respect to the entire 2022-2023\nassessment roll, for property located at 1000 Christopher Drive, in the\nhamlet of East Islip, town of Islip, county of Suffolk,\n\nSection 2 is the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nExisting law authorizes tax exemptions to be granted after the taxable\nstatus date has passed if a bill is chaptered authorizing the assessor\nto accept the late application.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS9126 Passed Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
